      "narration": "https://dnznrvs05pmza.cloudfront.net/text_to_speech/5c0ce715-c190-4369-ae34-961b5b34b2ba/What_a_manager_is__You_are_a_manager_now__and_here_is_what_that_means__in_plain_words__Before__your_.mp3?_jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJrZXlIYXNoIjoiZmFmYzRlOWYyMTg0ODRmNyIsImJ1Y2tldCI6InJ1bndheS10YXNrLWFydGlmYWN0cyIsInN0YWdlIjoicHJvZCIsImV4cCI6MTc4OTIxOTk5OX0.iY1MfY551-GxN58uRURSkv-JT_q-i53rK9P3jWlOwg0",
      "text": "What a manager is. You are a manager now, and here is what that means, in plain words. Before, your job was your own work. Now your job is your team\u2019s work, and the people who do it. That is the whole change, and it is a big one. Three things are new. One: you decide. What matters this week, who does what, and what waits. If you do not decide, the loudest request decides for you. Two: you approve. Timecards, time off, expenses, and requests now come to you, and Vanderbilt trusts your signature, so look before you sign. Three: you are responsible for people. Fair treatment, a safe place to speak up, a chance to grow, and the right help when life happens. You do not have to know everything. You have an HCM, an Engagement Consultant, a leave office, and a micro module for every common task. What you do have to do is show up as the manager: decide, approve, and take care of the people. And one thing a manager is not: the person who does everyone\u2019s work. When you are tempted to just do it yourself, that is the moment to manage instead. Next: five ideas the best-known voices on management agree on."
    },
