      "narration": "https://dnznrvs05pmza.cloudfront.net/text_to_speech/82e66da2-6de1-49ac-92c4-9cde0eecd30b/MVF5_video_relations.mp3?_jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJrZXlIYXNoIjoiYWNiZDQ4MGMzNGE1ZTZmNSIsImJ1Y2tldCI6InJ1bndheS10YXNrLWFydGlmYWN0cyIsInN0YWdlIjoicHJvZCIsImV4cCI6MTc4OTIyODMwMH0.fYRifhKEvrCiZbUSi_cKKnOSsjmHQ2LQmbkLVi6DO0M",
      "text": "Job two: take care of your people. Why it matters: people stay, and do their best work, for a manager who notices them. This is where your team\u2019s engagement is made or lost. Four habits. Listen and help: someone mentions a hard week at home; you listen, move what you can, and check in on Monday. And know the line: if they mention leave, a health issue, or unfair treatment, send it to the right office the same day, and never ask for a diagnosis. Grow them: once a quarter, without a form, ask what each person wants to be doing in two years, and find one assignment that stretches toward it. Thank them: the way you handled the vendor call on Thursday kept us on schedule, said on Friday. Specific, by name, that week. Great job everyone thanks nobody. Trust them: hand over the decision, not just the task, and ask the team before you set a new process. What to stop doing: being friendly instead of helpful, and saving growth for the annual review. This week: thank one person for one specific thing. Now flip the cards, then turn the page."
